# S-IVB APS engines (TRW TR-204 attitude, 150 lbf; Rocketdyne SE-7-1 ullage,
# 70 lbf): NASA CEA input deck, one run for both (they share the chemistry
# and the chamber pressure; their area ratios are not known).
# Run by tools/make_exhaust_table.py; the specs take the frozen expansion.
#
# p,psia: 100, the attitude engines' nominal (AS-501 FER §7.12: "the nominal
#   69 N/cm2 (100 psia)": H); taken for the ullage engine too (L).
# Propellants: N2O4 and MMH (MSFC-MAN-503 §6: H); o/f 1.6 (enginehistory.org
#   8.30, read through a search extract: M; AS506Data's feed ratio is 1.611).
# supar: 40 for the attitude engine and 9 for the ullage engine, guesses by
#   kin (the R-4D's 40:1, the SE-8's 9:1: L).
reac
  fuel=CH6N2(L) wt%=100 t(k)=298.15
  oxid=N2O4(L)  wt%=100 t(k)=298.15
prob case=APS rocket p,psia=100 o/f=1.6 eql frozen nfz=2 supar=9,40
output siunits trace=1e-5
end
